WEBVTT

00:00:01.190 --> 00:00:04.360
In order to cheer up Pierrot, who
was grief-stricken over his father’s death,

00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:07.400
Azuma Kazuma promised him that he would make a bread

00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:10.990
delicious enough to send him to heaven
at the final match of the Monaco Cup.

00:00:10.990 --> 00:00:13.070
<i>Japan</i> #61.

00:00:13.070 --> 00:00:15.410
And it’s called... Cannabis <i>Japan</i>!

00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:19.410
I’ll be sure to transport you to heaven.

00:00:19.410 --> 00:00:21.410
So, be sure to meet your father once again.

00:00:22.290 --> 00:00:25.500
When I think that I’ll be able to
meet both my mother and father...

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:27.670
I can’t keep my happiness in check.

00:00:27.670 --> 00:00:28.840
Mother?!

00:00:29.420 --> 00:00:30.670
That’s right!

00:00:30.670 --> 00:00:36.090
Azuma’s opponent, Shadow White, has promised to send me to the other end of the universe,

00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:41.140
where I’ll be able to meet my
mother who’s become a star.

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:44.650
The third round of the Monaco Cup finals.

00:00:44.650 --> 00:00:48.020
Finally, the battle is about to begin!

00:00:49.990 --> 00:00:52.240
There’s English bread, German bread, and French bread,

00:00:52.240 --> 00:00:54.160
but Japan’s bread, <i>Japan</i>, does not exist.

00:00:54.160 --> 00:00:56.530
In that case, there’s no choice but to create it.

00:00:56.530 --> 00:00:59.980
This story is a serious, biographical ballad of a boy who possesses Solar Hands,

00:00:59.980 --> 00:01:05.170
Azuma Kazuma, who will create a Japanese bread made by and for the Japanese people,

00:01:05.170 --> 00:01:09.050
which can be presented to the world proudly.

00:02:40.880 --> 00:02:43.220
All the ultimate ingredients collected!!

00:02:43.220 --> 00:02:45.350
The greatest finals in all of history!

00:02:50.350 --> 00:02:52.520
This is it, Leol-sama.

00:02:53.230 --> 00:02:54.980
Th-This is my mother?

00:02:54.980 --> 00:02:56.110
Yes.

00:02:56.110 --> 00:03:03.320
23 years ago, while giving birth to you,
she passed away in exchange for your life.

00:03:03.320 --> 00:03:07.500
The Queen of Monaco, Lady Maetel Leonhart.

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:08.540
Mother...

00:03:08.540 --> 00:03:13.040
The name Maetel comes from Greek, and apparently it means “mother.”

00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:21.180
But tragically, in the end, Maetel-sama was not able to embrace you, her beloved son.

00:03:21.510 --> 00:03:22.930
What’s this book?

00:03:22.930 --> 00:03:25.470
It was her favorite book.

00:03:25.470 --> 00:03:27.810
It is “Night on the Galactic Railroad,”

00:03:27.810 --> 00:03:32.980
by Japan’s exemplary poet and
author of fairy tales, Miyazawa Kenji.

00:03:33.660 --> 00:03:35.950
Mother was reading the original text?

00:03:35.950 --> 00:03:38.940
Yes. I guess she must have really liked it.

00:03:38.940 --> 00:03:44.630
I’m sure it was her wish to read it to you, Leol-sama.

00:03:45.790 --> 00:03:46.920
Mother.

00:03:46.920 --> 00:03:49.050
I wanted to meet you just once.

00:03:49.050 --> 00:03:52.460
I wanted to listen to you reading me Miyazawa Kenji.

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:05.180
Tournament Hall of the 3rd Round of the Monaco Cup Finals
Grand Casino

00:04:05.190 --> 00:04:07.180
Sorry for the wait, everyone.

00:04:08.190 --> 00:04:13.070
And now we’ll have the third round of
the finals of the Second Monaco Cup.

00:04:13.070 --> 00:04:16.060
Azuma Kazuma, the Japanese representative.

00:04:17.200 --> 00:04:18.570
Pierrot is floating.

00:04:18.570 --> 00:04:22.450
And his opponent is Shadow White,
the American representative.

00:04:24.620 --> 00:04:28.840
The theme of the third round is a bread that
best expresses the taste of your homeland.

00:04:28.840 --> 00:04:35.000
So, they must make breads that express the taste of Japan and America respectively.

00:04:35.590 --> 00:04:38.140
The judge and referee is me,

00:04:38.140 --> 00:04:42.170
one-time criminal, to be crowned as King of Monaco tomorrow...

00:04:43.020 --> 00:04:44.510
Pierrot!

00:04:44.510 --> 00:04:48.220
Pierrot! Criminal! Pierrot! Floating!

00:04:48.580 --> 00:04:50.690
He’s really popular.

00:04:50.690 --> 00:04:52.240
Yeah, you said it.

00:04:52.240 --> 00:04:54.450
So, then...

00:04:55.230 --> 00:04:56.730
Begin the match!

00:05:02.280 --> 00:05:03.780
Whoa!

00:05:03.780 --> 00:05:06.780
What amazing handling of the dough!

00:05:07.590 --> 00:05:08.340
He’s right!

00:05:08.340 --> 00:05:10.780
That’s the technique of a super veteran baker!

00:05:12.630 --> 00:05:16.290
The bread that Shadow is making is probably... a bagel!

00:05:16.720 --> 00:05:18.390
A bagel?!

00:05:18.390 --> 00:05:23.050
In regular breads like butter rolls, you
have 70 parts of water for 100 parts of flour.

00:05:23.580 --> 00:05:25.480
But, in hard breads like bagels,

00:05:25.480 --> 00:05:28.100
you have 50 parts of water for 100 parts of flour,

00:05:28.100 --> 00:05:29.740
so it’s very hard to knead.

00:05:30.540 --> 00:05:32.610
To be able to knead it at that speed...

00:05:32.610 --> 00:05:35.270
It’s impossible for an ordinary human being.

00:05:35.760 --> 00:05:37.320
How can this be?!

00:05:37.320 --> 00:05:40.280
Can Azuma win against that kind of monster?

00:05:40.280 --> 00:05:41.530
Did you see that?

00:05:41.530 --> 00:05:44.120
This is the #1 technique in the world.

00:05:44.120 --> 00:05:48.280
And I copied it 100% to make it my technique.

00:05:50.540 --> 00:05:51.840
Oh?!

00:05:51.840 --> 00:05:54.710
Azuma seems to be adding in a white liquid.

00:05:54.710 --> 00:05:58.050
That’s the liquid extract of cannabis seeds,
also known as cannabis milk, right?

00:05:58.050 --> 00:06:00.050
Huh? Oh, that’s right.

00:06:00.050 --> 00:06:03.850
Cannabis milk is extracted from cannabis seeds
and therefore falls in the vegetable food category.

00:06:03.850 --> 00:06:07.770
It has a natural sweetness and refreshing taste to it.

00:06:07.770 --> 00:06:11.060
You can drink it at Restaurant Asa in Shimokitazawa.

00:06:11.060 --> 00:06:13.780
So, you guys should try going there sometime.

00:06:13.780 --> 00:06:16.160
Let’s go Shimokitazawa!

00:06:18.220 --> 00:06:21.830
And so Shimokitazawa becomes famous worldwide...

00:06:21.830 --> 00:06:23.270
Azuma is great...

00:06:23.270 --> 00:06:24.200
You’re naive!

00:06:24.200 --> 00:06:26.040
Look at Shadow.

00:06:26.040 --> 00:06:29.210
He’s about to start with an
even greater trick, Kawachi-san.

00:06:29.210 --> 00:06:30.280
What was that?!

00:06:35.460 --> 00:06:37.160
T-This is...

00:06:37.160 --> 00:06:38.120
Rice?

00:06:38.840 --> 00:06:41.380
But, it doesn’t seem to be regular rice...

00:06:42.160 --> 00:06:43.630
What in the world is...?

00:06:44.890 --> 00:06:47.390
To think that the great Pierrot doesn’t know... Pathetic.

00:06:47.390 --> 00:06:48.840
Hey, Ryou!

00:06:49.190 --> 00:06:50.930
I heard that!

00:06:51.440 --> 00:06:54.620
How dare you insult the king?!

00:06:55.360 --> 00:06:57.780
If you don’t even know what that rice is...

00:06:57.780 --> 00:07:00.450
you’re being presumptuous in
calling yourself the King of Monaco,

00:07:00.450 --> 00:07:01.950
who’s supposed to be an expert on
ingredients from around the world.

00:07:01.950 --> 00:07:03.060
Oh?

00:07:03.830 --> 00:07:10.090
Everyone! It seems this guy here
wants to explain it instead of your king.

00:07:13.540 --> 00:07:14.630
Very well.

00:07:14.630 --> 00:07:17.880
I’ll explain instead of your worthless king.

00:07:17.880 --> 00:07:19.380
That rice is metzuru.

00:07:19.380 --> 00:07:22.580
The legendary sticky rice that’s a specialty of Sakata city in Yamagata prefecture.

00:07:22.580 --> 00:07:24.760
What’s metzuru?

00:07:24.760 --> 00:07:26.840
What’s a legendary sticky rice?

00:07:26.840 --> 00:07:28.810
He got us good.

00:07:28.810 --> 00:07:31.390
To think that he’d bring out metzuru...

00:07:31.390 --> 00:07:32.550
Yeah...

00:07:32.980 --> 00:07:34.860
It possesses a luster like silk...

00:07:34.860 --> 00:07:36.730
It’s soft, yet firm.

00:07:36.730 --> 00:07:41.910
The sekihan and daifuku made from it are considered to be among the best in the world.
Note: daifuku = sticky rice cakes stuffed with red bean paste

00:07:41.910 --> 00:07:43.450
But, it is hard to cultivate.

00:07:43.450 --> 00:07:47.490
Since it doesn’t grow anywhere except on the soil
found at the outskirts of Ennouji in Sakata city...

00:07:47.490 --> 00:07:50.070
it’s not found very much around the world.

00:07:50.070 --> 00:07:51.330
Oh I see...

00:07:51.330 --> 00:07:54.500
To think that we’d get to see
Japan’s legendary sticky rice in Monaco...

00:07:54.500 --> 00:07:55.580
That’s wonderful!

00:08:00.260 --> 00:08:01.880
But, Shadow...

00:08:01.880 --> 00:08:05.590
This theme requires you to make a bread that expresses the taste of your homeland.

00:08:07.590 --> 00:08:09.890
No matter how delicious it is,

00:08:09.890 --> 00:08:14.090
if you use rice only found in Japan,
I really can’t accept it.

00:08:14.560 --> 00:08:15.190
That’s right!

00:08:15.190 --> 00:08:18.020
That sticky rice can only be used for a <i>Japan</i>.

00:08:18.020 --> 00:08:20.240
Don’t worry.

00:08:20.240 --> 00:08:23.410
Instead of water, I’ll be using this.

00:08:23.410 --> 00:08:25.530
This is an ingredient developed in America!

00:08:25.530 --> 00:08:27.060
Rice Dream!

00:08:27.520 --> 00:08:29.040
Rice Dream?

00:08:29.040 --> 00:08:31.540
It’s not well-known in Japan, but...

00:08:31.540 --> 00:08:34.280
It’s a health drink that became a big hit in America.

00:08:34.960 --> 00:08:37.750
It’s a low-fat drink made from unmilled rice.

00:08:37.750 --> 00:08:40.630
It has safflower oil and sea salt added to it.

00:08:40.630 --> 00:08:43.220
It has a refreshing taste.

00:08:43.220 --> 00:08:45.140
Since Americans face a battle with obesity,

00:08:45.140 --> 00:08:48.130
I saw a lot of them drinking it
when I was studying there.

00:08:48.620 --> 00:08:50.180
America is a country of immigrants.

00:08:50.180 --> 00:08:53.730
If doesn’t have a long history, nor does it
have foods that can be called traditional.

00:08:53.730 --> 00:08:57.770
Most things can be traced back to
England, Germany, Italy and even Japan.

00:08:57.770 --> 00:09:00.140
Thus, I’m at a big disadvantage with this theme.

00:09:01.190 --> 00:09:02.740
I understand that quite well.

00:09:02.740 --> 00:09:05.910
But, the origins of the bagel are in New York.

00:09:05.910 --> 00:09:09.580
It is, without doubt, an original
bread that represents America perfectly.

00:09:10.220 --> 00:09:11.620
Okay, very well!

00:09:11.620 --> 00:09:15.500
I will accept your bagel, made with Rice Dream,
as being representative of your home country.

00:09:15.500 --> 00:09:17.200
Thank you.

00:09:18.130 --> 00:09:21.420
I thought that we could make use of his
weakness there, but I guess it didn’t work.

00:09:21.420 --> 00:09:25.470
That stuff that Azuma is mixing in
seems to be some sort of seasoning...

00:09:26.220 --> 00:09:27.370
I guess this is what I was looking for...

00:09:27.370 --> 00:09:29.250
Is that salt or something?

00:09:30.260 --> 00:09:34.010
That’s the signal fire of Azuma’s counterattack.

00:09:34.010 --> 00:09:37.070
All right. This is where things really start.

00:09:42.650 --> 00:09:45.650
Shadow just put his bagel into a boiling pot!

00:09:45.650 --> 00:09:47.660
Why are you so surprised?

00:09:47.660 --> 00:09:50.160
You normally boil bagels in water.

00:09:50.160 --> 00:09:51.570
In tea!

00:09:51.570 --> 00:09:52.690
In tea?!

00:09:54.870 --> 00:09:56.120
And this fragrance...

00:09:56.120 --> 00:09:57.120
Sniff sniff...

00:09:57.120 --> 00:09:58.200
This tea is...

00:09:59.670 --> 00:10:02.840
This is the legendary traditional English tea,

00:10:02.840 --> 00:10:04.540
Quality Season.

00:10:05.020 --> 00:10:06.720
Quality Season.

00:10:06.720 --> 00:10:09.550
Made by picking the best tea leaves in the best season.

00:10:09.550 --> 00:10:15.360
A legendary tea that involves the revival of a
manufacturing process from the Victorian era.

00:10:16.020 --> 00:10:21.350
The refined fragrance and mild flavor of this
tea are considered to be the best in the world.

00:10:21.350 --> 00:10:23.320
If I’m to boil the dough in this tea,

00:10:23.320 --> 00:10:27.280
the world’s best fragrance and the
world’s best flavor will be absorbed,

00:10:27.280 --> 00:10:31.060
making the world’s best bagel.

00:10:31.060 --> 00:10:32.450
I’m really surprised.

00:10:32.450 --> 00:10:34.950
Yeah? To think that he’s boiling it in tea...

00:10:34.950 --> 00:10:38.120
No, Shadow can talk even when he’s not imitating people!

00:10:38.120 --> 00:10:39.080
Oh that.

00:10:39.080 --> 00:10:42.080
All right. The last step now.

00:10:50.640 --> 00:10:53.170
With this, I’ll be winning effortlessly.

00:10:53.700 --> 00:10:54.470
Whoa!

00:10:54.470 --> 00:10:57.170
This time Shadow is deep-frying the bagel!

00:10:57.170 --> 00:10:59.100
What’s he doing?!

00:10:59.100 --> 00:11:01.890
I’d understand if it’s a doughnut, but why
in the world would he deep-fry a bagel?

00:11:01.890 --> 00:11:04.470
It’s in order to bring out the flavor of the metzuru.

00:11:05.230 --> 00:11:08.190
If you bake breads that have sticky rice like metzuru kneaded in,

00:11:08.190 --> 00:11:10.390
the bread will end up becoming
very hard, like a roasted rice cake.

00:11:10.390 --> 00:11:11.660
That’s why Shadow...

00:11:11.660 --> 00:11:14.530
No, Kirisaki must have disliked that,

00:11:14.530 --> 00:11:16.910
and came up with a way of bringing *
out the texture of the metzuru itself.

00:11:16.910 --> 00:11:20.650
And he must have chosen to deep-fry it after boiling it.

00:11:26.000 --> 00:11:27.680
Done.

00:11:28.010 --> 00:11:29.970
He’s already done?

00:11:29.970 --> 00:11:34.670
Compared to him, Azuma has
just begun to bake it in the oven.

00:11:35.350 --> 00:11:37.640
Is he going to be all right?

00:11:37.640 --> 00:11:39.670
What’s wrong, Kawachi-san?

00:11:39.670 --> 00:11:45.140
T-This is my intuition as a
person from Kansai, and not a baker.

00:11:46.190 --> 00:11:47.820
I can tell.

00:11:47.820 --> 00:11:51.190
That bagel will produce an incredible reaction!

00:11:52.690 --> 00:11:55.330
Come, King Pierrot!

00:11:55.330 --> 00:11:58.190
Please judge this <i>Gopan</i> bagel!

00:11:58.500 --> 00:12:01.200
And fly off to the ends of the universe!

00:12:01.200 --> 00:12:06.030
Please go and meet your
mother who has become a star...

00:12:22.300 --> 00:12:26.560
If I can meet Mother after eating the <i>Gopan</i> bagel...

00:12:26.560 --> 00:12:27.900
Gulp.

00:12:28.270 --> 00:12:31.060
I couldn’t be happier.

00:12:31.060 --> 00:12:32.530
Okay...

00:12:44.240 --> 00:12:47.490
Chuga-chug-chug.

00:12:50.000 --> 00:12:52.130
Blow away the unripe walnuts.

00:12:52.130 --> 00:12:54.500
Blow away the sour quince as well.

00:12:55.460 --> 00:12:56.500
You are...?

00:12:57.300 --> 00:12:59.260
My name is hard to pronounce.

00:12:59.260 --> 00:13:00.550
It’s Campanella.

00:13:00.550 --> 00:13:02.220
Campanella?

00:13:02.220 --> 00:13:04.050
Yeah, it’s really hard to pronounce.

00:13:04.050 --> 00:13:05.600
Let’s go, shall we?

00:13:05.600 --> 00:13:07.440
Go? Where?

00:13:08.560 --> 00:13:10.770
To the other end of the universe.

00:13:10.770 --> 00:13:13.490
By getting onto that galactic railway.

00:13:20.030 --> 00:13:21.820
Without losing to the rain...

00:13:21.820 --> 00:13:23.570
And without losing to the wind...

00:13:23.570 --> 00:13:26.330
And without losing to the snow,
or to the heat of summer.

00:13:26.330 --> 00:13:28.030
Hey, is this...?

00:13:28.450 --> 00:13:30.370
This is the world of Miyazawa Kenji.

00:13:30.370 --> 00:13:34.040
It certainly is not the world of 999.

00:13:34.330 --> 00:13:35.500
Is that so?

00:13:35.500 --> 00:13:38.380
This is the world of Miyazawa Kenji
that my mother liked so much.

00:13:38.380 --> 00:13:41.050
Thank goodness it’s not ripped off another anime.

00:13:41.050 --> 00:13:45.600
Next, we come to the Southern Cross. Southern Cross.

00:13:45.600 --> 00:13:48.360
We’ll be stopping there for 15 minutes.

00:13:49.520 --> 00:13:51.520
Ahh, that’s Coalsack.

00:13:52.390 --> 00:13:54.600
It’s an opening in the sky.

00:13:54.600 --> 00:13:57.060
That is where the real heaven is.

00:13:57.060 --> 00:14:00.580
And that over there is your mother.

00:14:04.140 --> 00:14:06.820
Campanella, let’s go together, okay?

00:14:07.420 --> 00:14:10.160
Huh? Where did you go?

00:14:10.160 --> 00:14:12.830
Whom are you looking for, Pierrot?

00:14:13.250 --> 00:14:15.330
No, Leol...

00:14:15.330 --> 00:14:16.830
Wh-Who’s there?

00:14:16.830 --> 00:14:18.330
Could it be you, Mother?

00:14:18.330 --> 00:14:20.380
That’s right, Leol.

00:14:20.380 --> 00:14:22.220
I am your mother.

00:14:22.220 --> 00:14:24.090
Maetel Leonhart.

00:14:24.090 --> 00:14:25.890
M-Mother?

00:14:25.890 --> 00:14:27.680
But, where are you?

00:14:27.680 --> 00:14:30.180
I’m right here.

00:14:30.180 --> 00:14:31.720
Down below.

00:14:31.720 --> 00:14:32.890
Huh?

00:14:32.890 --> 00:14:33.810
Down?

00:14:33.810 --> 00:14:36.150
Welcome, Leol.

00:14:36.650 --> 00:14:38.570
There’s so many mothers!

00:14:38.570 --> 00:14:42.270
Could it be that this whole
star is made of you, Mother?

00:14:42.270 --> 00:14:44.320
Yeah, that’s right.

00:14:44.320 --> 00:14:47.620
Because after dying, I became a star.

00:14:47.620 --> 00:14:52.580
More importantly, since this is the first
time we’ve met, tell me about yourself.

00:14:52.580 --> 00:14:54.280
O-Okay.

00:14:57.290 --> 00:14:59.500
I wonder what happened to Pierrot-san?

00:14:59.500 --> 00:15:03.350
He stopped moving the
moment he ate the <i>Gopan</i> bagel.

00:15:04.020 --> 00:15:06.580
It’s happened exactly as I feared it would.

00:15:07.680 --> 00:15:12.270
And so, because the <i>Gopan</i> bagel was
so very delicious, I was able to come here.

00:15:12.270 --> 00:15:13.640
Hmm?

00:15:13.640 --> 00:15:14.730
What was that?

00:15:14.730 --> 00:15:16.930
Tell your mother here, too.

00:15:16.930 --> 00:15:19.690
So, like I said... The <i>Gopan</i> bagel was...

00:15:19.690 --> 00:15:20.770
Hmm? Huh?

00:15:20.770 --> 00:15:21.690
What was that?

00:15:21.690 --> 00:15:23.650
Tell your mother here, too.

00:15:23.650 --> 00:15:24.690
So, like I said...

00:15:24.690 --> 00:15:25.860
Hmm? Huh?

00:15:25.860 --> 00:15:26.740
What was that?

00:15:26.740 --> 00:15:27.360
So, like I said...

00:15:27.360 --> 00:15:28.160
Hmm? Huh?

00:15:28.160 --> 00:15:28.530
What was that?

00:15:28.530 --> 00:15:29.200
So, like I said...

00:15:29.200 --> 00:15:30.070
Hmm? Huh? What was that?

00:15:30.070 --> 00:15:30.960
So, like I said...

00:15:30.960 --> 00:15:31.260
Hmm? Huh? What was that?

00:15:31.260 --> 00:15:32.080
So, like I said...

00:15:32.080 --> 00:15:32.660
Hmm? Huh? What was that?

00:15:32.660 --> 00:15:34.290
So, like I said...

00:15:34.950 --> 00:15:38.170
Exactly how many times do I
need to repeat the same story?

00:15:38.170 --> 00:15:39.580
50,000 times.

00:15:39.580 --> 00:15:40.910
So many?!

00:15:40.910 --> 00:15:44.920
Because there’s 50,000 of me on this star.

