00:18:28.130 --> 00:18:32.550
Whoa. Azuma is deep-frying his doughnut as well.

00:18:32.550 --> 00:18:36.220
Yahoo! We’re not losing either!

00:18:36.220 --> 00:18:38.930
But, if it’s a doughnut, it’s obvious to deep-fry it.

00:18:38.930 --> 00:18:42.680
But, isn’t it odd that he’s frying it after baking it?

00:18:43.390 --> 00:18:44.390
Don’t you know?!

00:18:44.390 --> 00:18:46.780
Normally, if you’re making fried doughnuts,

00:18:46.780 --> 00:18:48.690
they’re definitely more delicious if fried after being baked.

00:18:48.690 --> 00:18:50.610
Oh, is that so?

00:18:50.610 --> 00:18:55.610
If you fry the raw dough without baking it,
then the dough will absorb a lot of oil.

00:18:55.610 --> 00:18:58.780
But once it’s baked, the
amount of oil absorbed is reduced.

00:18:58.780 --> 00:18:59.650
Oh...

00:18:59.650 --> 00:19:03.780
But, he’s not doing something that simple.

00:19:10.040 --> 00:19:11.210
